! mcp_bootstrap_p228.strap -- MCP printed page 228: the Input Program's
! V SET/V COM/V MD routines, the V RQEXT constant, the V IN* entries and
! V WTTS (lines 1-56).
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.235, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID CA000655  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 228"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 224673, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines, every one located, contiguous from 224673.00 to
! 224727.40 (a half word; next word 224730.00).  The volume OCR puts
! printed p.227's last row at 224672.40 and p.229's first at 224730.00,
! so the page joins on both sides.  Remarks run -0654 .. -0704: none on
! lines 22, 46-49, 55, 56; -0675 and -0699 are never printed; line 44
! prints "-0697+".  A lone "-" prints left of the remark column on
! lines 45 and 50-54.  Asterisks print after the LOCATION on lines 13
! and 36.
!
! PRINTED FORMS THE ASSEMBLER NOW TAKES:
!  * Line 21 "V+ICR,V T3,.V F" -> 000000.57 07: V F is the bit address
!    .32, and a point in front of a symbolized bit address has no effect
!    on it (C22-6578 printed p.64, A4.8.2(c)) -- the same .57 lines 1
!    and 6 print for "V+ICR,V T3,V F".
!  * Line 44 "V IN2  SIC,V SQ1" (224721.00 -> 224322.00 80) is followed by
!    line 45's LV on a separate card (serials 0A000698 / 0A000699): a SIC
!    whose next half word is not a branch, which IBM's STRAP assembled.
!  * Line 56 SIC,(V P) at 224727.40 is the last row; its branch is
!    p.229 line 1 (224730.00) -- the p.131 straddle: carried as a
!    comment, no !CHECK (a SIC with nothing after it is still refused).
!
! GLYPHS.  The NAME/STATEMENT O prints squared with a straight left
! side and reads C: "V CCM", "V CCM2" (VCOM is how the landed decks
! spell p.228 l.15), "V INCN", "V INCFF", "V NCP".  V NCP is VNOP by
! binary (224157.63 = landed VNOP 224157.40 + .23); V INON at 900 dpi
! is an unmistakable O; V INOFF rests on ink (the same glyph as NCP's
! O, not the round C of SC5A beside it) -- nothing references it.
! V RQEXT: Q with its tail at 900 dpi (the sheet read RGEXT).
! Octal-field opens (C00000, .1C, .5C) are 0.  Hex bytes written 0 for
! an open round: line 16 "C5" (V+I,V T5,0 -> 05), line 20 "C1" (= lines
! 12/14/25's B,(V P) 01), line 47 "CC" (B, with no index is 00), line
! 48 "BC" (= p.221's M+1,V TSQ second half word B0) -- settled by what
! the statement assembles to.  Line 27 "B7" read 87 at 400 dpi and is
! B at 900 dpi (straight left stem, as line 18's B7).  Line 13/16's last operand "C" is 0.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials 0A000655 .. 0A000709 (prefix as
! p.221 records it; the header prints CA000655).  Lines 46/47 share
! 0A000700 (SIC,YTSTR + B,YTST on one card); otherwise one per line.
!
! External symbols not landed come from this page's binary, as noted.

VF      SYN, .32                     ! p.213 line  6 "V F SYN,.32"
